        "subject": "LU-10606 lod: store HSM attributes in a layout mirror",
        "message": "LU-10606 lod: store HSM attributes in a layout mirror\n\nThe HSM attributes of a file are kept in the \"trusted.hsm\" xattr,\napart from its layout, so FLR and PCC cannot see that a file has an\narchive copy, nor that the copy is out of date.\n\nStore them in a data-less foreign mirror of the layout instead, as\nPCC-RO does, with type \"posix\", the HSM state flags and the archive ID\nand version.  lod.*.hsm_layout selects where they are stored when they\nchange: 0 for \"trusted.hsm\" (the default until 2.19.53), 1 for the\nlayout, -1 for both.  A file without a layout keeps them in the xattr.\nLOD reads the mirror first, then the xattr, returns both as\n\"trusted.hsm\", also for a remote object, and lists them for a local\none, so the MDD, MDT, coordinator, changelogs, HSM release, restore\nand migration, and tools that read the xattr are unchanged.  The\nattributes move to the selected place the next time they change, and\nare removed from the other one.\n\nOnly adding or removing the mirror changes the layout generation, as a\nclient takes a new generation after a failed restore for a restored\nfile.  Keep the HSM mirror of a file when its layout is replaced by a\nswap, as the attributes do not move with the layout, also with\nhsm_layout=0, and refuse to split it from the file.  It is not\nresynced by \"lfs mirror resync\", and a write marks it stale but leaves\nHS_DIRTY to be set at close with its changelog record.  PCC-RO adds a\nmirror of its own and does not use the HSM one.\n\nDescribe the tunable in lod.hsm_layout(4).  Add sanity-hsm test_1g,\ntest_1h and test_1i for HSM in the layout, and sanity-pcc test_54 for\nPCC-RO on an archived file.\n\nTest-Parameters: fortestonly testlist=sanity-hsm,sanity-pcc\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I18ee438a4d767b7c5b8dc5a6293e00f85f3ebbe5\n"
      },
